 System Hardening with Bash Scripts
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create automated Bash scripts to implement Linux system hardening measures
Configure firewall rules using UFW and iptables
Secure SSH configurations through scripting
Implement user account security policies
Verify and test system hardening implementations
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command line operations
Familiarity with text editors (nano or vim)
Understanding of file permissions and ownership
Basic Bash scripting knowledge
Access to sudo privileges
